{% doc %}
  Emits the per-carousel colour custom properties as an inline `style` value.

  ## The colour model

  Arrow and dot colours already exist in every colour scheme —
  `slider_arrow_icon`, `slider_arrow_background`, `slider_arrow_border`, their
  hover pairs, `slider_indicator_color` and `slider_indicator_active_color`. A
  merchant who changes a scheme changes every carousel in the store, which is
  what a scheme is for.

  So this snippet emits nothing at all unless the section asks for custom
  colours. That is the point: the default path costs zero bytes per section, and
  only a merchant who wants this one carousel to differ pays for the override.

  ## Three spellings of the same question

  Sections say it one of three ways, and all of them are read here:

      carousel_inherit_scheme  checkbox — on inherits, off overrides. The
                               current spelling, and the same control
                               `blocks/group.liquid` uses for the same idea.
      carousel_color_source    select — `inherit` | `custom`
      carousel_custom_colors   checkbox — the original spelling, inverted

  The checkbox wins wherever a section has one, then the select, then the old
  checkbox. Nothing had to be converted for this snippet to keep working, and a
  section can be moved to the current spelling one at a time.

  Note the inversion: `carousel_inherit_scheme` is true when colours are
  *inherited*, and `carousel_custom_colors` is true when they are *not*. Reading
  them as one flag is how the two would quietly swap over.

  ## A scheme first, then the pickers

  **Colour scheme** re-declares the eight slider properties from whichever
  scheme the merchant picked — not by putting `color-scheme-container` on the
  carousel, which would paint that scheme's background behind the cards as well.
  Only the controls change.

  The individual pickers below it are layered on top of that, so a merchant can
  take a scheme and correct one colour in it rather than filling in all eight.
  Each one is emitted only when it has a value, which is what makes the layering
  work: an empty picker leaves the scheme's answer standing.

  ## Gradient

  `carousel_nav_style` can be `gradient`, which paints the arrow background from
  `carousel_nav_gradient` instead of a flat colour, and the progress bar to
  match. Border and icon stay flat — a gradient border needs `border-image`,
  which cannot follow a `border-radius`, and a gradient icon needs the
  `background-clip: text` trick that makes an 18px glyph illegible.

  Parameters:
    settings (object, required)  Section settings

  @example
    <swiper-carousel style="{% render 'carousel-style', settings: section.settings %}">
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign inherit = settings.carousel_inherit_scheme
  assign color_source = settings.carousel_color_source

  assign use_custom = false
  if inherit != nil
    unless inherit
      assign use_custom = true
    endunless
  elsif color_source == blank
    if settings.carousel_custom_colors
      assign use_custom = true
    endif
  elsif color_source == 'custom'
    assign use_custom = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if use_custom -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign nav_style = settings.carousel_nav_style | default: 'solid'
    assign scheme = settings.carousel_color_scheme
  -%}
  {%- capture custom_colors -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The whole set, or none of it. Half a scheme — arrows from one, dots from
      the section's — is a combination no merchant asked for and no preview
      shows them before they publish.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if scheme != blank and scheme.settings != blank -%}
      --color-slider-arrow-icon: rgb({{ scheme.settings.slider_arrow_icon.rgba }});
      --color-slider-arrow-background: rgb({{ scheme.settings.slider_arrow_background.rgba }});
      --color-slider-arrow-border: rgb({{ scheme.settings.slider_arrow_border.rgba }});
      --color-slider-arrow-icon-hover: rgb({{ scheme.settings.slider_arrow_icon_hover.rgba }});
      --color-slider-arrow-background-hover: rgb({{ scheme.settings.slider_arrow_background_hover.rgba }});
      --color-slider-arrow-border-hover: rgb({{ scheme.settings.slider_arrow_border_hover.rgba }});
      --color-slider-indicator: rgb({{ scheme.settings.slider_indicator_color.rgba }});
      --color-slider-indicator-active: rgb({{ scheme.settings.slider_indicator_active_color.rgba }});
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if settings.carousel_nav_icon_color != blank -%}
      --color-slider-arrow-icon: {{ settings.carousel_nav_icon_color }};
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.carousel_nav_border_color != blank -%}
      --color-slider-arrow-border: {{ settings.carousel_nav_border_color }};
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.carousel_nav_icon_hover != blank -%}
      --color-slider-arrow-icon-hover: {{ settings.carousel_nav_icon_hover }};
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.carousel_nav_border_hover != blank -%}
      --color-slider-arrow-border-hover: {{ settings.carousel_nav_border_hover }};
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Solid and gradient write different properties, so the unused one is left
      undeclared rather than set to `none` — the stylesheet's `var()` fallback
      is what picks the scheme colour back up.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- case nav_style -%}
      {%- when 'gradient' -%}
        --carousel-nav-background: {{ settings.carousel_nav_gradient | default: 'var(--gradient-primary)' }};
        --carousel-nav-background-hover: {{ settings.carousel_nav_gradient_hover | default: settings.carousel_nav_gradient | default: 'var(--gradient-primary)' }};
        --carousel-bar-background: {{ settings.carousel_nav_gradient | default: 'var(--gradient-primary)' }};
      {%- else -%}
        {%- if settings.carousel_nav_bg != blank -%}
          --color-slider-arrow-background: {{ settings.carousel_nav_bg }};
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if settings.carousel_nav_bg_hover != blank -%}
          --color-slider-arrow-background-hover: {{ settings.carousel_nav_bg_hover }};
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcase -%}

    {%- if settings.carousel_dot_color != blank -%}
      --color-slider-indicator: {{ settings.carousel_dot_color }};
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.carousel_dot_active_color != blank -%}
      --color-slider-indicator-active: {{ settings.carousel_dot_active_color }};
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {{- custom_colors | strip_newlines | strip -}}
{%- endif -%}
